COMMIT: a88e81f at 2025-10-30 09:19:03 - fix: Task 1E Phase 1 - Fix dependency injection in WeightTrackingView

**WHAT:** Fixed duplicate WeightManager creation (Consultant Review Finding #1)

**HOW:**
1. Refactored WeightTrackingViewModel to use empty init()
   - Changed managers from `let` to `var!` (late initialization)
   - Moved loadGoalSettings() out of init into configure()
   - Added configure() method to inject @EnvironmentObject managers
2. Updated WeightTrackingView to call configure() in .onAppear
   - Passes @EnvironmentObject managers after SwiftUI injection completes
   - Maintains MVVM architecture with proper dependency injection
3. Verified fix with all 217 tests passing (including 21 WeightManager tests)

**EXPECTED:**
- Single WeightManager instance shared across app via @EnvironmentObject
- No duplicate manager creation in ViewModel init
- All existing tests continue to pass

**ACTUAL:** ✅ CONSULTANT ISSUE #1 FIXED
- WeightTrackingViewModel no longer creates duplicate WeightManager
- Proper dependency injection via configure() after @EnvironmentObject available
- SwiftUI limitation bypassed (init before environment injection)
- All 217 tests passing (WeightManagerTests: 21/21 ✅)

**Technical Details:**
- SwiftUI @StateObject init happens BEFORE @EnvironmentObject injection
- Solution: Empty init() + configure() called from .onAppear with env managers
- Pattern: Late initialization with implicitly unwrapped optionals (safe in this context)

**Files Changed:**
- FastingTracker/Core/ViewModels/WeightTrackingViewModel.swift
  - Lines 11-22: Changed managers to var! with documentation
  - Lines 54-71: Empty init() + configure() method
- FastingTracker/UI/Views/WeightTrackingView.swift
  - Lines 204-212: Added configure() call in .onAppear
- FastingTrackerTests/ThreadSafety/WeightManagerThreadSafetyTests.swift
  - Line 125: Removed unused weak self capture
  - Line 355: Added trailing newline

